<div id="2026-11-22-focus-acl-roletier" class="cl-entry">
<h3>2026-11-22 — Today's Focus no longer dumps every todo to members; staff are not guests in JS</h3>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>What.</strong> On /planning/daily, logged-in members and normal users now see only todos they own, are assigned, reported, or posted. Developers see programming todos (or their own), not the HelpDesk/ops list. HelpDesk staff see helpdesk/admin-classified todos (or their own), not the full programming backlog. CSC admins still see every site through the existing filter. HelpDesk staff such as helpdesksupport are no longer treated as guests in <code>ComservConfig.roleTier</code> (they are members, and cannot pick privileged models).</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Why.</strong> HelpDesk CSC-20260915-9174 (security slice only; ranking and AI:Tune were not changed). Two holes: the Focus queue used "general" as a pass for every logged-in role, so members saw an owner-scale dump; and staff roles were missing from the role-tier map, so the chat widget thought helpdesksupport was a guest even after the page loaded.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Files.</strong> <code>lib/Comserv/Util/FocusRanking.pm</code>, <code>lib/Comserv/Controller/Planning.pm</code>, <code>lib/Comserv/Util/ModelCatalog.pm</code>, <code>root/static/js/local-chat.js</code>, <code>t/util_focus_ranking_acl.t</code>, <code>t/util_model_catalog_roles.t</code></p>
</div>
